=== REASONING ===

This is a verification-only terminal slice. It can only prove what
the predecessor slices have built. The Phase-50 methodology delegates
two responsibilities to each feature slice (0011..0064):

  (a) Implement the AI surface (handler, hook, UI, jobs, etc.) behind
      the AI-Off Contract guards.
  (b) Contribute its Routes / UI test IDs / job-name metadata into
      `internal/ai/features/registry.go` so the final gate can iterate
      over EVERY feature and prove I1, I5, I6, I7, I12 for it.

Slices 0001..0010 build the foundation (provider abstraction, settings,
ai_call_log, tool framework, SSE, eval harness, embeddings, redaction,
rate limiter). Slices 0011..0037 ship 27 features (chatbot through
auto-name unnamed locations). Slices 0062..0064 ship the 3 ML predictive
features. That leaves slices 0038..0061 — 24 features in the
G/X/S/M/P/V/PU/GEN series — unimplemented.

Without those 24 slices landed:

- `features.Registry` is missing 24 entries.
- `features.CoverageOK()` (the explicit §4a precondition) will not
  cover those 24 surfaces — they have no metadata, so the loop
  silently skips them. A "PASS" with only 40 of 64 surfaces enumerated
  is exactly the false-green this Covenant exists to prevent.
- `TestBaselineEndpointParity` cannot prove that 24 unimplemented
  surfaces leave the baseline untouched, because there is no contrast
  to measure (off vs all-AI-on collapses to off vs 40-AI-on).
- `TestZeroProviderEgress_OffMode` would only soak the 40 active
  features; there is no signal it would block egress added by a
  later feature slice.
- The audit report's headline "Slices completed: 64 / 64" is
  unachievable.

Per ADR-015 §I11 ("final-gate proof"), Phase-50 closes only when
end-to-end auditable proof of all 12 invariants exists across all
features. With 24 features absent, that proof literally cannot be
constructed. Forcing the gate to run anyway would either crash on
missing registry entries or, worse, return a misleading PASS that
covers only 62.5% of the surface area the Phase commits to guard.

The correct, honest action — encoded in this slice's Blocked Path —
is to stop, log the predecessor gap, and commit only the blocked
log so the next operator picks up at slice 0038 (G2 Suggest New
Geofences) instead of being told (incorrectly) that Phase-50 is
closed.

Forward path to unblock this gate:

  1. Land slices 0038..0061 in order (24 feature slices, each
     producing its own STATUS=DONE log + registry contribution).
  2. Re-run slice 0065 (W1 SPA wiring) — currently blocked on the
     same 24 missing slices; it should turn green automatically
     once its inputs exist.
  3. Re-run this slice (9999 final gate) — predecessor coverage
     check will then pass at 64/64 and the §2..§5 verification
     can execute against a complete registry.

